  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Pattern: Xが{渇|かわ}く.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{渇|かわ}いている indicates a current state of being thirsty.\n\nWRITING:\n{渇|かわ}く and {乾|かわ}く are both read かわく but have different meanings. {渇|かわ}く means \"to be thirsty\" or \"to crave,\" while {乾|かわ}く means \"to dry\" or \"to become dry.\" In practice, {喉|のど}が{渇|かわ}く and {喉|のど}が{乾|かわ}く are both used for thirst, but {渇|かわ}く emphasizes the craving while {乾|かわ}く emphasizes the physical dryness.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {喉|のど}が{渇|かわ}く (to be thirsty)\n- {愛情|あいじょう}に{渇|かわ}く (to crave affection)\n- {知識|ちしき}に{渇|かわ}く (to thirst for knowledge)",
